    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0485" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.77/59.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President promises to see that consideration of the railroad bill is deferred
                    to the next Congress, the present one being about to adjourn.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
